WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.509
Those of you who watched our Don’t buy a
MacBook Just yet video and decided to wait

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:09.230
to buy a MacBook, Congratulations, because
Apple has just released a couple of new MacBooks

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.230
this morning!

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.630
So in this video, we’re gonna go through
everything that’s changed with these new

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:17.570
MacBooks and we’ll recommend which 2019
MacBook you should buy depending on your needs.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.570
We’ll also talk about the rumored 16”
MacBook Pro.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.680
For starters, Apple has quietly got rid of
the $1300 12” Retina MacBook and the old

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.080
$999 MacBook Air, so their lineup is much
more simple now.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.619
And this morning, Apple has released a new
13” MacBook Air with nothing but the addition

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:38.280
of some display tech and a $100 price reduction
to $1099, which is awesome news for users

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.930
who need a budget MacBook.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:45.609
Apple has also finally updated the lower-end
13” MacBook Pro after two long years, bringing

00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:50.600
it from a dual-core processor to a quad-core,
as well as bringing the Touch Bar as standard

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.760
for the same $1299 price.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.670
Now I’ve got to call this an incredible
value.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:58.960
And if you’re a student, you can pick one
of these up for $100 less and get a free pair

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.300
of Beats headphones with Apple’s back to
school sale, which we’ll link to in the

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.300
description.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.180
The only thing that’s changed on the MacBook
Air is the addition of True Tone technology,

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.390
which adjusts the white balance of the display
to match your surroundings.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.310
I personally love this feature since it’s
easier on the eyes when you’re in a warm-lit

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:16.310
room.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:20.030
The new low-end MacBook Pro released this
morning gets True Tone as well, along with

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:24.180
a bunch of other upgrades like getting the
Touch Bar with Touch ID, and getting Apple’s

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.390
T2 chip, which is great for security, video
encoding and automatic storage encryption.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:33.650
It’s now packing a new 8th gen quad-core
processor which is clocked lower than the

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:37.920
old dual-core, but it will definitely be a
lot faster with hyperthreading and a pretty

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.920
high turbo boost.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.210
It’s also getting a bump up to Iris Plus
645 integrated graphics, which will perform

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:49.900
somewhere in between the old 640 and 655 graphics
that comes in the $1800 MacBook Pro.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.450
We’ll be getting our hands on both of these
new MacBooks soon, so if you want to see us

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.859
test them, click subscribe right now so you
don’t miss those videos!

00:01:56.859 --> 00:02:00.920
Neither of them are packing Apple’s rumored
new scissor keyboard, they’re still packing

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.270
the butterfly keyboard, which should be updated
with the new, more reliable materials like

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.050
we saw on the high-end 2019 MacBook Pros.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:12.130
On the plus side, if you’re still worried
about the keyboard, Apple has added both new

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:15.940
MacBooks to their keyboard repair program,
so if you have any issues, Apple will fix

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.940
them for free.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.310
We’re still expecting Apple to announce
the 16” MacBook Pro with the new scissor

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:25.090
keyboard later this year, maybe in September
or October, so if you’re looking to buy

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.650
a high-end MacBook Pro, you should probably
wait.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:31.490
But for everyone else who was waiting for
an update to the lower-end MacBooks, here’s

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.940
everything that’s different between the
new MacBook Air and the new MacBook Pro.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.620
The MacBook Air has 2 hours of extra battery
life.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:41.080
The MacBook Pro will have much better processor
and graphics performance.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.550
The Pro has a brighter 500 nit display and
a much more color accurate display than the

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:48.113
Air, with P3 wide-color gamut, just like the
higher-end MacBook Pros.

00:02:48.113 --> 00:02:52.550
The Pro also has better speakers than the
Air, and it comes with Bluetooth 5.0, while

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.280
the Air sticks to 4.2.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.390
The Air gets the Hey Siri feature while the
Pro doesn’t, but I always turn it off anyway

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.370
since I don’t really care for it.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.129
The Air’s keyboard is also sloped downward
so you get a more comfortable typing experience,

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.340
but the Pro has a larger trackpad, which I
personally love.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:13.940
The Pro gets a much faster 61W charger compared
to 30W on the Air, and of course, the Pro

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:19.750
is $200 more expensive, which means you can
get 256GB of storage on the Air for the same

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.470
price as the 128GB MacBook Pro.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:26.980
However, the Pro is packing an incredible
value this year, and we would strongly recommend

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:30.239
anyone who can afford the Pro to buy it over
the Air.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:35.420
In fact, the $1800 MacBook Pro is not that
much better than the new low-end model.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:40.250
It just gets Hey Siri support, an extra two
Thunderbolt 3 ports, slightly faster graphics,

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.069
and faster quad-core processors, that’s
it.

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:47.659
How much storage you choose is up to you,
but we’d recommend at least 256GB if you

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:50.510
love to deal with a lot of files and do work
on your MacBook.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.190
And now that we have a more complete lineup
of MacBooks this year, let’s begin with

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.540
our 2019 MacBook buyer’s guide.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:00.420
If you just need a basic MacBook for doing
things like using the internet, using web-based

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.370
apps, doing basic school or business work,
and streaming shows and movies on the internet,

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.780
then the MacBook Air will be perfect for you.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.310
It gets more battery life, and you’ll save
a good amount of cash.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.340
And you’ll probably be fine with 128GB of
storage unless you really like storing photos

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.340
and files.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:20.220
Now if you need a bit more performance or
you do entry-level professional work, then

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.650
the new $1299 MacBook Pro is for you.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.470
It packs a better and brighter display which
is great for things like photo editing, and

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:30.630
now that it has a quad-core processor, faster
graphics performance and Apple’s T2 chip,

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.950
it can actually do basic 4K or HEVC codec
video editing.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:40.050
The quad-core processor may be clocked at
a lower 1.4GHz compared to the $1800 MacBook

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:45.520
Pros 2.4GHz processor, but the turbo boost
speeds are almost the same, so there may not

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.610
actually be a massive difference between the
two.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:51.980
And the extra processing power means you’ll
get more out of a powerful eGPU setup, which

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.350
we’ll definitely be testing soon, so make
sure to subscribe now.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:59.290
Getting an eGPU means you may actually be
able to do some high-end video editing and

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.540
get a ton of extra gaming performance.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.760
So the new low-end 13” MacBook Pro is perfect
for an eGPU setup.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.810
So now for the $1800 MacBook Pro, who should
buy it?

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:12.850
Well, if you’re someone who really needs
the extra processing power, like for higher-end

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:18.200
photo editing, using Logic, or coding, then
you’ll gain from the higher-end 13” MacBook

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.200
Pro.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.620
The biggest reason to upgrade to that model,
however, is for the two extra Thunderbolt

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.750
3 ports.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.880
If you know you’ll need the extra ports,
then you should definitely get that model

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:27.880
instead.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:33.370
And it already comes with a 256GB SSD, so
in reality, you’re actually paying just

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.320
$300 more for better performance.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.260
And finally, we have the 15” MacBook Pro.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:42.350
If you love large displays, or you want a
lot more performance, with it’s standard

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:48.130
6-core i7 processor, a dedicated graphics
chip, faster RAM and more of it, then you

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.390
should definitely buy the 15” MacBook Pro.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:54.160
This is great for video editors who don’t
want to buy an eGPU, or anyone else who wants

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.270
some extra power for their professional work.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:00.070
It also comes with better speakers, a larger
trackpad and a faster charger.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:04.990
Now if you want a very high-end MacBook Pro,
like in the $3000 range, we strongly recommend

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:08.890
that you wait a couple of months for the 16”
MacBook Pro announcement that we’re all

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:09.890
expecting.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:13.990
It’s gonna be expensive, but we think it’ll
feature the long-awaited full redesign of

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:18.810
the MacBook Pro, with a new, better keyboard
and a better display with thinner bezels.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:23.070
And it seems like that redesign could carry
over into the rest of the MacBook lineup within

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.490
the next year or two, where we may see the
switch to Apple’s new ARM processors.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.900
So there you have it guys, if this video helped
you make a buying decision, hit that like

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:34.040
button and click the circle above to subscribe
so you don’t miss out when we get these

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.590
new MacBooks in our office.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:40.380
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video.

